{%- comment -%}
  Section: siwa-editorial | Owner: A-05 | Task: ST-06

  Phlur's slot 3, measured: a 200px quiet band — one centred statement in an
  800px measure, no imagery, at most a small attribution. It is the page
  taking a breath between two commerce rows, and it stays that quiet. A band,
  not a story section.

  WHY IT CARRIES BRAND COPY — deviation D-3.
  The feature bible's Gap 6, "is this brand real or just packaging?", is the
  only one of the six trust gaps with no homepage placement anywhere in the
  bible. Phlur's slot 3 is a brand statement. Filling it with Siwa's own Our
  Story copy closes that gap without inventing a section phlur does not have.

  NOTHING HERE IS HARDCODED.
  Every string is a schema setting. The defaults are seeded from the audit's
  content/our-story.md and content/about-us.md — a schema default may be a
  literal, markup may not — and each one renders only when it is non-blank,
  so a merchant who empties the eyebrow, the attribution or the link simply
  gets a shorter band rather than an empty element.

  There is no locale-key fallback in this section, and that is deliberate
  rather than an omission: locales/en.default.json carries `sections.oracle`,
  `sections.tester_invite`, `sections.product_row` and `sections.collections`
  but no `sections.editorial` namespace, and ST-06 may not add keys. A `| t`
  on a key that does not exist in both dictionaries is a validator error, so
  the fallback here is "render nothing" rather than "render a broken key".
  See the report — the seed for `sections.editorial.*` is ST-10's to write.

  A QUIET BAND SPENDS NO GOLD.
  `cta_variant` offers text, quiet and secondary and nothing else. The hero
  above and the Oracle invite below each spend the fold's one gold CTA
  (principle 1); a third gold on the breath between them would halve all
  three signals. The link is also never a bare "Learn more" — the default
  label names its destination (DESIGN.md §8 anti-pattern 11).

  THE DARK SCHEME IS THE THEME'S EXISTING BAND, NOT A NEW PALETTE.
  `dark` adds the `.on-dark` class and nothing else. siwa-tokens.css re-points
  the semantic ink tokens under `.on-dark`, and siwa-themes.css re-expresses
  that band per design direction through its --band-* tokens, so the band
  follows whichever preset is live and is checked by tools/check-contrast.mjs
  like every other pair. This file declares no colour of its own for it.

  No JavaScript, no imagery, no behaviour. The section is type on a ground.
{%- endcomment -%}

{{ 'siwa-editorial.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

{%- liquid
  assign s = section.settings

  assign band_class = 'siwa-editorial__band siwa-editorial__band--' | append: s.color_scheme
  if s.color_scheme == 'dark'
    assign band_class = band_class | append: ' on-dark'
  endif

  assign rhythm_class = 'siwa-editorial__inner--' | append: s.rhythm
  assign align_class = 'siwa-editorial__measure--' | append: s.alignment

  assign has_cta = false
  if s.cta_label != blank and s.cta_url != blank
    assign has_cta = true
  endif
-%}

{% style %}
  {%- comment -%}
    The measure is re-pointed through --measure, the design system's own
    line-length token, rather than through a bespoke property: .siwa-prose
    already reads it, so the statement, its paragraphs and any link inside
    them all bound to the merchant's width with no extra selector. The CSS
    file clamps it with min(100%, …) so no media query is needed for it.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .siwa-editorial__measure {
    --measure: {{ s.max_width }}px;
  }

  {%- comment -%}
    Gate 0 finding F2. The rhythm itself is a CLASS, not an inline value,
    because siwa-editorial.css lowers it inside @media (max-width: 768px) and
    an `#shopify-section-… { padding-block }` rule would outrank that media
    query at every viewport — the trap siwa-footer.liquid documents for its
    `columns` setting and .siwa-grid fell into before it.

    So this block emits only the two OFFSET custom properties. They are
    composed into the rhythm by the class rule in the stylesheet, which means
    the desktop pair below and the mobile pair inside the query are the same
    property at the same specificity: source order decides, and the media
    query is second. Nothing here can win at a width it was not written for.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .siwa-editorial__inner {
    --siwa-editorial-pad-start: {{ s.padding_top }}px;
    --siwa-editorial-pad-end: {{ s.padding_bottom }}px;
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .siwa-editorial__inner {
      --siwa-editorial-pad-start: {{ s.mobile_padding_top }}px;
      --siwa-editorial-pad-end: {{ s.mobile_padding_bottom }}px;
    }
  }
{% endstyle %}

<div class="{{ band_class }}">
  <div class="siwa-container siwa-editorial__inner {{ rhythm_class }}">
    <div class="siwa-editorial__measure {{ align_class }}">
      {%- if s.eyebrow != blank -%}
        <p class="siwa-label siwa-editorial__eyebrow">{{ s.eyebrow }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if s.statement != blank -%}
        <div class="siwa-editorial__statement siwa-prose">{{ s.statement }}</div>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if s.attribution != blank -%}
        <p class="siwa-editorial__attribution siwa-body-sm siwa-muted">{{ s.attribution }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if has_cta -%}
        <div class="siwa-editorial__actions">
          {%- render 'siwa-button',
            label: s.cta_label,
            href: s.cta_url,
            variant: s.cta_variant
          -%}
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Editorial statement",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "siwa-editorial",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Content"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "One statement, one measure, no imagery. This band is the breath between two product rows — if it needs a picture or a second paragraph it has stopped being this section."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "eyebrow",
      "label": "Eyebrow",
      "info": "Two or three words. Leave blank to omit it.",
      "default": "Our story"
    },
    {
      "type": "richtext",
      "id": "statement",
      "label": "Statement",
      "info": "The band's voice. Concrete — the oasis, the workshop, where it is made. Not adjectives about luxury (DESIGN.md §7.1).",
      "default": "<p>A bouquet of carefully selected perfumes, inspired by the beauty and charm of Siwa Oasis. Made in Egypt to international standards.<\/p>"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "attribution",
      "label": "Attribution",
      "info": "A name or a place, set small under the statement. Leave blank to omit it.",
      "default": "Siwa Fragrances"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "cta_label",
      "label": "Link label",
      "info": "Name the destination — \"Read our story\", never \"Learn more\" (DESIGN.md §8 anti-pattern 11). The link renders only when it has both a label and a destination.",
      "default": "Read our story"
    },
    {
      "type": "url",
      "id": "cta_url",
      "label": "Link destination"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "cta_variant",
      "label": "Link treatment",
      "info": "No gold here. The folds above and below this band already spend the page's gold CTAs, and principle 1 rations it to one per fold.",
      "options": [
        { "value": "text", "label": "Text link" },
        { "value": "quiet", "label": "Quiet button" },
        { "value": "secondary", "label": "Outline button" }
      ],
      "default": "text"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Appearance"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "color_scheme",
      "label": "Ground",
      "info": "Ink inverts the band through the design system's .on-dark tokens, which each design direction re-expresses, rather than through colours of its own.",
      "options": [
        { "value": "page", "label": "Page — the same ground as the rows around it" },
        { "value": "surface", "label": "Surface — one step up from the page" },
        { "value": "dark", "label": "Ink — inverted band" }
      ],
      "default": "surface"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "alignment",
      "label": "Alignment",
      "options": [
        { "value": "center", "label": "Centred" },
        { "value": "start", "label": "Start of the line" }
      ],
      "default": "center"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "max_width",
      "label": "Statement width",
      "info": "A long line is harder to read than a short one — the eye loses its place on the return sweep. 800px is the measured reference; past about 900 the band stops reading as a single held sentence.",
      "min": 480,
      "max": 1120,
      "step": 20,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 800
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Layout & spacing"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "rhythm",
      "label": "Vertical rhythm",
      "info": "DESIGN.md §4 alternates commerce and ceremonial rhythm down the page. This band is the ceremonial beat between two --tight product rows, so it takes Section. The values come from the active design direction and drop on their own below 768px.",
      "options": [
        { "value": "section", "label": "Section — ceremonial" },
        { "value": "tight", "label": "Tight — commerce" }
      ],
      "default": "section"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding_top",
      "label": "Extra padding top",
      "info": "Added on top of the rhythm above, not instead of it.",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 96,
      "step": 4,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 0
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding_bottom",
      "label": "Extra padding bottom",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 96,
      "step": 4,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 0
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "mobile_padding_top",
      "label": "Extra padding top (mobile)",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 96,
      "step": 4,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 0
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "mobile_padding_bottom",
      "label": "Extra padding bottom (mobile)",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 96,
      "step": 4,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 0
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "Editorial statement"
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
